            <div xml:id="d35-a4">

                <pb facs="0135" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg47"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Subenclosure 3—Telegram—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Political
                            Department to the Swiss Legation at
                            Washington
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p>O. F. 40. At the urgent request of the Austro-German Government would you hand
                    the Government of the United States the following communication: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Entente troops have occupied the Bacska South Hungary where there are
                            important grain supplies. Besides the Czecho-Slovac troops have occupied
                            a part of Upper Hungary where there are large quantities of potatoes.
                            The quickest aid which Entente can give the German-Austrian provinces
                            (which) lacking in food stuffs would consist in, sending in advance
                            grain and potatoes from these provinces to Vienna.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi>,] November 22, 1918.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
